# --- The Ur-Ghast's dark tower. Every name below is Benimatic's own, verbatim from the 1.15.4
# archive's lang/en_US.xml.
#
# ⚠️ Upstream's key for the wood is `tile.TFTowerStone.*` while the class is BlockTFTowerWood and every
# display name says "Towerwood". The key is a fossil from an earlier version where the tower was made
# of stone; the names are what players know, so the names are what is kept and the key follows this
# port's own naming instead.
#
# The five towerwood variants are five blocks here (upstream: one block, five metadata), so each gets
# a plain `.name`.
tile.twilightforest.tower_wood.name=Towerwood Planks
tile.twilightforest.tower_wood.encased.name=Encased Towerwood
tile.twilightforest.tower_wood.cracked.name=Cracked Towerwood
tile.twilightforest.tower_wood.mossy.name=Mossy Towerwood
tile.twilightforest.tower_wood.infested.name=Infested Towerwood

# The device is ONE block with fourteen states, so its names are keyed by metadata --
# BlockLogicTFTowerDevice.getLanguageKey appends the number, which is the same shape upstream's
# `tile.TFTowerDevice.<meta>.name` has. Six of the fourteen are reachable from the creative menu; the
# rest are only ever seen for the instant the block is in that state.
#
# ⚠️ Upstream tags four of these [WIP] -- the two ghast trap states and the two reactor states -- and
# the tag is dropped from the name here, following the precedent set for the magic saplings. The
# blocks genuinely do nothing, and blocks.lang says so plainly rather than hiding it behind an
# abbreviation.
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.0.name=Reappearing Block
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.1.name=Active Reappearing Block
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.2.name=Vanishing Block
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.3.name=Active Vanishing Block
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.4.name=Locked Vanishing Block
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.5.name=Unlocked Vanishing Block
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.6.name=Tower Builder
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.7.name=Active Tower Builder
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.8.name=Inactive Tower Builder
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.9.name=Anti-builder
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.10.name=Ghast Trap
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.11.name=Active Ghast Trap
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.12.name=Carminite Reactor
tile.twilightforest.tower_device.13.name=Active Carminite Reactor

# ⚠️ Benimatic spells it "Carminie Reactor" in en_US.xml and "Carminite" everywhere else in the mod --
# the ore, the item, the golem. It is a typo in one string rather than a second material, so the name
# above is the corrected spelling. This is the only place in the tower's strings where his text is not
# reproduced literally, and it is recorded here so it is not "fixed" back.

# The translucent block is unobtainable and appears in no menu, so these names are only ever seen
# through a debug readout. They exist upstream and cost five lines.
tile.twilightforest.tower_translucent.0.name=Reappearing Block
tile.twilightforest.tower_translucent.1.name=Active Reappearing Block
tile.twilightforest.tower_translucent.2.name=Built Tower Block
tile.twilightforest.tower_translucent.3.name=Active Built Tower Block
tile.twilightforest.tower_translucent.4.name=Anti-built Block
